# SPA fallback for React Router on Cloudflare Pages / Netlify.
#
# Without this rule, refreshing on any client-side route (e.g.
# /dashboard/brand/raqm/identity, /b/acme/assets) returns a 404 because
# the host looks for a file at that path. With this rule, the host
# serves /index.html for any unknown path and React Router resolves the
# route in the browser.
#
# Vite copies anything in `public/` into `dist/` automatically, so this
# file ships as `dist/_redirects` after build — exactly where Cloudflare
# Pages and Netlify look for it. No further config needed.
#
# See docs/ux-redesign/EXECUTION.md and the hosting plan for context.

/*    /index.html   200
